@page
@model CommunityHub.Pages.Organizer.SoMeCadenceModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Posting frequency";
}

@* 🔴 §1207 — THIS PAGE NO LONGER GOVERNS ANYTHING, SO IT NO LONGER PRETENDS TO.

   Operator 2026-09-12: *"if i define 3 rounds, we must plan 3 rounds"* — reported as a bug, and the
   cause was two controls for one number. §1195 moved rounds onto the category rules ("fold in the
   frequency page"), and the planner has read those ever since. This page kept a second, editable
   number and a sentence claiming *"The engine plans the campaign from these"*, which by then was
   false: saving here changed a row nothing read.

   🔑 Leaving an editable control that does nothing is the §1178 defect — a setting with readers and
   no effect, or here an effect with no readers. The honest move is to say where the number lives and
   send him there, rather than delete the route someone may have bookmarked. *@

<div class="card">
    <h1>Posting frequency</h1>

    @if (Model.AccessDenied)
    {
        <p class="error">@Localizer["Common.OrganizersOnly"]</p>
    }
    else
    {
        <p>
            <strong>How many rounds each category runs now lives with the rest of its rules</strong> —
            beside that category's start date, its round dates and its end date, on one page.
        </p>
        <p>
            <a class="btn" asp-page="/Organizer/SoMeSettings">Open SoMe settings</a>
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
            Each category there has a round count, a date per round and an <strong>Add a round</strong>
            button. A round you add — or simply give a date to — is planned on the next run.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
            <strong>Nothing already scheduled is affected by a change.</strong> A lower number means
            fewer new posts, never the removal of posts you have approved or edited.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
            Type 5 has no frequency setting on purpose: <strong>the dates come from your deck</strong>,
            one scheduled run per date you wrote. To change when they go out, change the deck and
            re-import, or move a single post in
            <a asp-page="/Organizer/SoMePostEditor">Edit posts</a>.
        </p>
    }
</div>
